June 5, 2025 [ 354 ]
After leaving office, Musk criticized the Trump administration's Big Beautiful Bill , calling it a "disgusting abomination" due to its provisions increasing the deficit. [ 355 ] A feud began between Musk and Trump, with its most notable event being Musk alleging Trump had ties to sex offender Jeffrey Epstein on X (formerly Twitter) on June 5, 2025. [ 356 ] [ 357 ] Trump responded on Truth Social stating that Musk went "CRAZY" after the "EV Mandate" was purportedly taken away and threatened to cut Musk's government contracts. [ 358 ] [ 359 ] Musk then called for a third Trump impeachment. [ 360 ] The next day, Trump stated that he did not wish to reconcile with Musk, and added that Musk would face "very serious consequences" if he funds Democratic candidates. [ 361 ] On June 11, Musk publicly apologized for the tweets against Trump before deleting them, saying they "went too far". [ 362 ]
